{"name":"Digital","hex":"#636365","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"digital","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having to do with digits (fingers or toes); especially, performed with a finger.","Property of representing values as discrete, often binary, numbers rather than a continuous spectrum."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A digital option.","Digital equipment or technology."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/digital"}],"entries":[{"title":"Neobank","blocks":[{"text":"A neobank is a type of direct bank that operates exclusively using online banking without traditional physical branches. In contrast to direct banks, in many cases, neobanks do not have their own banking licenses, and instead rely on partner banks. They typically have lower operational costs, which can sometimes result in lower fees and more competitive interest rates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Community_Noun_project_39956.svg/330px-Community_Noun_project_39956.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neobank"},{"title":"Digital Equipment Corporation","blocks":[{"text":"Digital Equipment Corporation, using the trademark Digital, was a major American company in the computer industry from the 1960s to the 1990s. The company was founded by Ken Olsen and Harlan Anderson in 1957. Olsen was president until he was forced to resign in 1992, after the company had gone into precipitous decline."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Assabet_Woolen_Mill_-_Maynard%2C_Massachusetts_-_DSC04913.jpg/330px-Assabet_Woolen_Mill_-_Maynard%2C_Massachusetts_-_DSC04913.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_Equipment_Corporation"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Maynard_MA_Clock_Tower_Place.jpg/500p